From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] use schedule(static) for libsharp's dynamic OpenMP loops

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around a libgomp defect on the riscv64 runners, riseproject-dev/python-wheels#617]

CI's cp314 leg segfaulted inside libgomp during map2alm (PR #2430,
run 36393265628, job 108833715006): "Fatal Python error: Segmentation
fault" with the C stack landing in
healpy.libs/libgomp-*.so.1.0.0 -> healpy.libs/libsharp-*.so.2.0.2 ->
libgomp again, from test_sphtfunc.py::test_map2alm_pol. cp313 built
and tested clean on the same commit, matching gotcha 166's signature
for the runners' libgomp exactly: a fault inside the OpenMP runtime,
intermittent across otherwise-identical jobs, and specific to the
dynamic/guided work-share schedules.

cextern/healpix vendors libsharp (src/common_libraries/libsharp), and
it schedules its four spherical-harmonic-transform loops --
map2phase, phase2map and the alm/coefficient loop in
sharp_execute_job (sharp.c), plus the root-finder in
sharp_legendre_roots.c -- with schedule(dynamic,*). Every one of them
runs on every map2alm/alm2map call, which is why the crash isn't
confined to one test. sharp_mpi.c's own schedule(dynamic,1) is left
alone: it lives entirely behind #ifdef USE_MPI, which this build never
defines, so it never compiles into the wheel.

Moving these four loops to schedule(static) costs load balancing on
transforms whose per-ring cost varies (each ring's associated Legendre
function evaluation scales with its colatitude-dependent mmax), not
correctness. Tag it Inappropriate and revert once the runners'
toolchain is fixed, per gotcha 166.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp.c                | 6 +++---
 cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp_legendre_roots.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp.c b/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp.c
index 59e4638..6ed28c9 100644
--- a/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp.c
+++ b/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp.c
@@ -767,7 +767,7 @@ NOINLINE static void map2phase (sharp_job *job, int mmax, int llim, int ulim)
     ringhelper_init(&helper);
     int rstride=job->ginfo->nphmax+2;
     double *ringtmp=RALLOC(double,job->nmaps*rstride);
-#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,1)
+#pragma omp for schedule(static)
     for (int ith=llim; ith<ulim; ++ith)
       {
       int dim2 = job->s_th*(ith-llim);
@@ -812,7 +812,7 @@ NOINLINE static void phase2map (sharp_job *job, int mmax, int llim, int ulim)
     ringhelper_init(&helper);
     int rstride=job->ginfo->nphmax+2;
     double *ringtmp=RALLOC(double,job->nmaps*rstride);
-#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,1)
+#pragma omp for schedule(static)
     for (int ith=llim; ith<ulim; ++ith)
       {
       int dim2 = job->s_th*(ith-llim);
@@ -880,7 +880,7 @@ NOINLINE static void sharp_execute_job (sharp_job *job)
     sharp_Ylmgen_init (&generator,lmax,mmax,ljob.spin);
     alloc_almtmp(&ljob,lmax);
 
-#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,1)
+#pragma omp for schedule(static)
     for (int mi=0; mi<job->ainfo->nm; ++mi)
       {
 /* alm->alm_tmp where necessary */
diff --git a/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp_legendre_roots.c b/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp_legendre_roots.c
index ec81ecb..7a9a3c4 100644
--- a/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp_legendre_roots.c
+++ b/cextern/healpix/src/common_libraries/libsharp/libsharp/sharp_legendre_roots.c
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ void sharp_legendre_roots(int n, double *x, double *w)
 #pragma omp parallel
 {
   int i;
-#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,100)
+#pragma omp for schedule(static)
   for (i=1; i<=m; ++i)
     {
     double x0 = cos(pi * ((i<<2)-1) * t1) * t0;
-- 
